Considering the age and earning capacity of the deceased, the Tribunal fixed the monthly income of the deceased at Rs.20,000/- per month, adding 40% of the income towards future prospects, deducting 1/2 of the income towards personal expenses of the deceased, adopting the multiplier of '18' (7000 + 40%-2800; 7000 + 2800-9800; 9800-4900 (1/2) x 12 = 58800;
58800 x18 10,58,400/- and rounding it off, the Tribunal has arrived at a sum of Rs.10,58,000/-
towards loss of income.
